    "killington": {
      "status": "ok",
      "resort": "Killington",
      "adapter": "powdr",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-18 16:00:15",
      "note": "Evening, Beast fans, What an insanely fun day celebrating our season pass holders, enjoying some delicious food, and grooving to live jams. The snow was buttery soft, and the only worry was whether or not you forgot your sunscreen. Looking ahead, there’s a chance of showers late tonight and strong south winds setting the tone for tomorrow. On Sunday the Beast takes a turn with rain in the morning that flips to snow late morning, temps potentially dropping into the lower 30s, and maybe a few inches of snow stacking up with a steady breeze keeping things feeling wintry. The conditions off of the Superstar Six have been phenomenal with legit, soft bumps lining the center of Superstar and flowy lines on the sides while surfaces on Skyelark and Bittersweet are more cruisable. Both runs should offer similar conditions tomorrow, although the snow should feel heavier with bases slightly firmer as precip falls and temps dip lower. Ramshead will be dedicated to the park scene, with the Ramshead Quad spinning exclusively for Timberline Park access. Keep in mind, that terrain is standalone, so plan on hopping a shuttle or driving if you’re heading between Ramshead and K-1. The Parks Crew has been hard at work all week battling temps, and they’re rolling into the final weekend of Timberline with around 20 features ready to ride. Check the Terrain Parks Report for the full details on what we have available. Please note that there is no longer any beginner terrain available. Our grooming team will be smoothing out Upper Skyelark, Lower Bitterweet, and the terrain park on Timberline. We did what we could to stretch the shredding from the peak and it was a joy to carve down Double Dipper one last time. With conditions rapidly changing as they do in the Spring, be aware that coverage can change in a matter of hours and trails may have areas of spotty coverage. The Superstar Six is scheduled to spin starting at 8:00 a.m. tomorrow. With the way the weather has been going and is forecasted, today will be our last day on the K-1 Gondola, Snowdon Six, North Ridge Quad, and Canyon Quad. Sunday is planned to be our closing date for the Ramshead Quad and our Timberline Park. Stay tuned for updates on our spring park plans off of Superstar. Get out and make the most of this weekend! - Evan Operating Day: 159 Season passes for 26/27 are now on sale! Lock in the lowest price on Beast 365 or Winter Unlimited passes with lots of perks, plus free skiing & riding for the rest of this spring. And there's more good news for families: Youth & Child pass pricing has been significantly reduced for next season, with over $300 in savings available on Beast 365 access. Lifts Key lifts operate seven days a week from 9:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on Monday through Friday, and from 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on Saturday and Sunday. The North Ridge Quad opens at 9:30 a.m. on weekdays and 8:00 a.m. on weekends. The Superstar Six will close at 5:00 p.m. on April 18th, 25th, and May 2nd. Starting on May 3rd, the Superstar Six will be open Friday through Sunday while conditions allow. Upcoming lift closure dates: Snowdon Six - Saturday, April 18th K-1 Gondola - Saturday, April 18th North Ridge Quad - Saturday, April 18th Ramshead Express Quad - Sunday, April 19th The Tubing Park presented by bubly is closed for the season. Uphill Travel Uphill travel is now closed for this season. Please visit killington.com/uphill for full information on our uphill travel policies. MOUNTAIN SERVICES Parking & Shuttles Parking is available at the K-1 and Ramshead lodges. Vale Road and Vale Road parking lots are closed Monday - Friday for road work and on Saturday mornings to facilitate Snowdon Triple chair pickups. Please respect signage and allow our parking staff to assist you on your trip to the slopes. Shuttle service is available from 7:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. midweek and 6:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekends and holidays unless otherwise stated in this report. Winter car camping and overnight parking is only available in the lot across from Skyeship Lodge, though please note that the Skyeship Lodge is closed for this season. See details here . Lodge Services All lodges listed here are open daily from 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekdays and 7:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekends/peak dates*. K-1 Lodge Breakfast: Served starting at 8:30 a.m. on weekdays and 7:30 a.m. on weekends/peak dates. Lunch: Served from 10:30 a.m. - 3:00 p.m. daily with limited offerings midweek. Brew Bar (2nd floor): Open serving handcrafted coffees, cocktails, and beers starting at 9:00 a.m. daily. K-1 Pub (3rd floor): Open Saturday, April 18th and Sunday, April 19th before closing for the season. Rentals & Killington Sports at K-1: Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. Demos & Tuning: Available via the K-1 Rental Shop from April 10th through May 3rd. All pass holders—including Beast 365 and Unlimited—will receive 50% off demo rentals. Guest Services: 1st floor - Open 30 minutes before lifts until 1:00 p.m. on weekdays and until 4:30 p.m. on weekends/peak dates. 2nd floor - Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. Superstar Umbrella Bar: Open at 11:00 a.m. from Friday - Sunday offering beer, wine, liquor, and specialty hot cocktails. Ramshead Lodge Breakfast: Served starting at 8:30 a.m. on Fridays and 7:30 a.m. on weekends/peak dates. Lunch: Served daily with grab & go options & soups. The pizza station is open Thursday - Monday, and the full grill menu is available Friday - Sunday. Guest Services: Open 30 minutes before lifts until 12:00 p.m. on Monday – Thursday and until 4:30 p.m. on Friday - Sunday at the ticket windows outside of the lodge. Rentals: Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. Child Care Center: Open Monday to Friday from 8:30 a.m. - 3:45 p.m. Closing Date: April 19th Bear Mountain Lodge - Closed for the season. Snowshed Lodge - Closed for the season. Snowshed Demos & Tuning remains open seven days a week, providing tuning services for guests and Season Tune holders. Demos also available with more options at K-1. Skyeship Lodge - Closed for the season. On-Mountain Dining Options : Peak Lodge – Closed for the season. Jerk Jamaican Mountain Grill – Closed for the season. Ledgewood Yurt – Closed for the season. Mountain services are subject to change. Please check here daily before making your lunch and lodge choices. Winter Lift Tickets and rentals must be purchased online at this link . Check to see if your pass is good to go using our Online Pass Checker . Find our Season Pass FAQs by clicking here . Season passes for summer 2026 and winter 26/27 are now on sale! Buy now . Have a ticketing question? Our text number ( 802-523-2202 ) is the best way to get it answered quickly, but please note that we cannot process transactions via text. Have a season pass question? Call 1-800-621-MTNS or email seasonpass@killington.com Please visit Killington.com/cancellation for more details on our cancellation policy. Killington Sports at Route 4 is open daily from 10:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Closing date: Sunday, April 19th Killington is a cashless resort. We accept all major credit cards as well as Apple, Google, and Samsung Pay. *No remaining Peak Dates during winter 2025/26. We strive to have the most up-to-date and accurate snow report, but errors can happen from time to time. If you have feedback or a correction for us, please share it here.",
